LICENCE SCOPE — dual licensing (MIT + BSL 1.1)
================================================================================
Pry is dual-licensed. Two scopes, one tree:

  MIT         Everything NOT listed as BSL-1.1 below: the core scraping engine,
              extraction, templates, MCP server, x402 payment rail, CLI, SDK,
              browser-extension/, wordpress-plugin/, shopify-app/,
              llm_providers/, and the bulk of api.py, mcp_production.py and
              x402.py. Full MIT text: the body of this file.

  BSL-1.1     The files enumerated in the SPDX-BSL-FILE-LIST block of
              LICENSE-BSL-STEALTH (40 files at the last check), each carrying
              "SPDX-License-Identifier: BSL-1.1" in its header. Entry points:
                src/pry/engine/ultimate_scraper.py   (10-tier fallback engine)
                src/pry/engine/stealth_engine.py     (stealth orchestration)
                src/pry/engine/stealth_scripts/*.js  (anti-detection injectors)
              Terms: LICENSE-BSL-STEALTH (Change Date 2029-01-01,
              Change License MIT).

The SPDX block in LICENSE-BSL-STEALTH is the authority, not this summary.
"python3 scripts/check_licence_spdx.py" fails when that block and the actual
file headers disagree in either direction; regenerate the block with
"python3 scripts/check_licence_spdx.py --list".

SPDX-License-Identifier for the tree as a whole: MIT AND LicenseRef-BSL-1.1
(the same expression pyproject.toml declares).
